  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nIssued 353 AM MDT WED AUG 5 2026\nStronger westerly flow aloft will move into the area as upper-\nlevel troughing builds offshore and the Desert Southwest ridge\nflattens and weakens. While hot temperatures will continue,\nincreased winds and the low possibility of precipitation return\nto the forecast. Current long range models keep the \nprecipitation primarily in far southern ID & along the ID/NV \nborder, which would manifest itself through afternoon \nthunderstorms. Precipitation chances generally increase day \nover day as monsoonal moisture is transported north. For now, \nit looks as though the rest of the Great Basin and Desert \nSouthwest will receive the precipitation, but our region is on \nthe cusp. Temperatures will be 5-10 degrees above normal with \nlower valleys near 100 degrees Saturday, decreasing to near \nnormal / about 5 degrees above normal Sunday onward. Breezy \nwinds and hot temperatures will create fire weather concerns. \nSmoky conditions will continue from area wildfires which may \nkeep temperatures slightly cooler than forecast.",
